    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR updates the regression runner to support parallel execution with a spinner-based UI, while also improving live output streaming for single-test runs. It also introduces a mechanism to avoid SimpleCov race conditions when tests are run concurrently.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add parallel execution mode for `--tag` and `--all` with per-job spinners and failure-only output.\n- Stream single-test output live via a custom `TTY::Command` printer.\n- Add `tty-spinner` dependency + Sorbet RBI, and gate SimpleCov with `COVERAGE=0` for parallel runs.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 4 out of 6 changed files in this pull request and generated 3 comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tools/test/regress-cli.rb | Implements job expansion, parallel workers + spinner UI, and live output streaming for single tests. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/test/test_helper.rb | Skips SimpleCov startup when `COVERAGE=0` to avoid parallel coverage races. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/udb/resolver.rb | Adds cross-process file locks around generated spec/resolve steps to reduce concurrent write hazards. |\r\n| sorbet/rbi/gems/tty-spinner@0.9.3.rbi | Adds Sorbet types for the new `tty-spinner` gem dependency. |\r\n| Gemfile | Adds `tty-spinner` dependency. |\r\n| Gemfile.lock | Locks `tty-spinner` and its dependencies. |\n</details>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Files not reviewed (1)</summary>\n\n* **sorbet/rbi/gems/tty-spinner@0.9.3.rbi**: Language not supported\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/riscv/riscv-unified-db/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
